# Build output. Regenerated by Gradle on every build, and by far the bulk of the tree
# (~378 MB against ~60 MB of actual source).
build/
*/build/
**/build/

# Gradle and Kotlin caches.
.gradle/
.kotlin/

# Native build cache from the NDK/CMake tasks. 130 MB, fully regenerated.
.cxx/
**/.cxx/

# Machine-specific: contains the absolute path to this machine's Android SDK, which is
# wrong for anyone else and is regenerated by Android Studio on first open.
local.properties

# IDE state.
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# Signing credentials. The keystore itself is kept outside the repository entirely, but
# these patterns exist so that a copy landing here by accident is not committed. Losing the
# key means never being able to update an existing install; leaking it means someone else
# can sign builds that Android treats as yours.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# JVM heap dumps. Gradle writes these next to the build when a task dies of an
# OutOfMemoryError, and they are the size of the heap that died -- the one committed by
# mistake in "Drop dead weight" was 644 MB, and had to be purged from history on
# 2026-09-10. Never worth keeping: they describe one crash on one machine.
*.hprof

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Deliberately NOT ignored, and worth saying why:
#   app/src/main/jniLibs/**/*.so  - the emulator cores. 36 MB, but they are not built from
#                                   this repo and cannot be regenerated from it, so a clone
#                                   without them cannot produce a working app.
#   core-backups/                 - previous core builds kept on purpose (see CHANGELOG.md);
#                                   the 2026-08-16 Beetle build in particular is not
#                                   otherwise recoverable.
